      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Three spellings, one root: <b>-cede</b> (<i>concede</i>, <i>precede</i>), <b>-ceed</b> (only <i>proceed</i>, <i>succeed</i> and <i>exceed</i>) and <b>-cess</b> (<i>excess</i>, <i>process</i>). <b>supersede</b> is the odd one out: it is spelled with an <i>s</i> because it comes from a different root, <i>sed</i> (sit), as in <i>sediment</i>. To supersede is to sit above, to replace."
